diff --git a/ambiguities/2025.yaml b/ambiguities/2025.yaml
index 82c7554..c99d012 100644
--- a/ambiguities/2025.yaml
+++ b/ambiguities/2025.yaml
@@ -2615,3 +2615,61 @@ register:
           individual care provider for caring for an eligible individual (whether related or unrelated) living in the provider’s
           home", "Ten qualified foster individuals under age 19, or", "Five qualified foster individuals age 19 or older"'
       status: Lane x2-paynow2 (coverage expansion, pay not on a W-2), 2026-11-15.
+    - id: amb.2025.f4952_no_2024_form
+      text_at_issue: 'f4952 p. 1, Part I, line 2: "Disallowed investment interest expense from 2024 Form 4952, line 7". A
+        filer who carried disallowed investment interest into 2024 and filed no 2024 Form 4952 (for example because the
+        standard deduction was taken for 2024) has no 2024 line 7 to read.'
+      readings:
+      - Ask only for an amount on line 7 of a 2024 Form 4952; such a filer answers No and enters no carryforward.
+      - Use the amount a 2024 Form 4952 would have shown on line 7 had one been completed (the carryforward, treated as 2024
+        investment interest, less the part the 2024 net investment income could have absorbed).
+      - Use line 7 of the latest Form 4952 filed.
+      chosen: The first (f4952.carryover asks only about a 2024 Form 4952), until the owner rules on a refusing question for
+        this case.
+      reason: 'Pub. 550: "You can carry over the amount of investment interest you could not deduct because of this limit to
+        the next tax year. The interest carried over is treated as investment interest paid or accrued in that next year."
+        The third reading carries the whole earlier amount past a year whose net investment income could have absorbed it,
+        so it can overstate line 2; it is not used. The second follows the quoted rule but asks the filer to complete a form
+        for a past year. The first can understate the deduction, for a filer whose 2024 net investment income did not
+        absorb the carryforward; it cannot overstate it.'
+      cite:
+        doc: p550
+        locator: 'p. 46, Limit on Deduction, "You can carry over the amount of investment interest you could not deduct
+          because of this limit to the next tax year. The interest carried over is treated as investment interest paid or
+          accrued in that next year."'
+      status: Planning lane plan-med-income (BUG-0833), redrafted in lane v2-income after the wording red team (A6),
+        2026-11-16; for the owner.
+    - id: amb.2025.amt_transient
+      text_at_issue: 'i6251 p. 8, Line 3: "A qualified dwelling for AMT is a house, apartment, condominium, or mobile home not
+        used on a transient basis." The instructions do not define "used on a transient basis".'
+      readings:
+      - A house, apartment, condominium or mobile home rented out for short stays is used on a transient basis, so its
+        mortgage interest is a line 3 adjustment; asked in s2.amt_boat, whose Yes refuses.
+      - Only a place run as lodging for passing guests, like a hotel, is meant; a second home that is sometimes rented
+        for short stays is a qualified dwelling.
+      chosen: The first.
+      reason: Every Yes to s2.amt_boat refuses (Form 6251), so the broader reading can lose a case but cannot give a wrong
+        value.
+      cite:
+        doc: i6251
+        locator: 'p. 8, Line 3, Mortgage Interest, "A qualified dwelling for AMT is a house, apartment, condominium, or mobile
+          home not used on a transient basis"'
+      status: Planning lane plan-med-income (BUG-0900), drafted in lane patch-inc-m34, 2026-11-16; for the owner.
+    - id: amb.2025.f8853c_line24_public
+      text_at_issue: 'i8853 p. 9, Line 24: "Enter the reimbursements you received or expect to receive through insurance or
+        otherwise for qualified LTC services provided for the insured for LTC periods in 2025." The instructions do not say
+        whether Medicaid or VA payments made straight to the care provider are reimbursements "through insurance or
+        otherwise".'
+      readings:
+      - They are; they count on line 24 and lower the cost-based limit on line 25.
+      - They are not; only payments under an insurance contract or a like arrangement count.
+      chosen: The first, as worded (the f8853c.line24 question follows i8853's "or otherwise" and names neither program).
+      reason: 'i8853 places no limit on "otherwise". If the second reading is right, a filer whose costs Medicaid or the VA
+        paid would overstate line 24 and so the taxable amount on line 26. Money family or friends gave toward the care is
+        excluded in the help: it is not a reimbursement of the filer''s costs (inferred).'
+      cite:
+        doc: i8853
+        locator: 'p. 9, Line 24, "Enter the reimbursements you received or expect to receive through insurance or otherwise for
+          qualified LTC services provided for the insured for LTC periods in 2025"'
+      status: Planning lane plan-med-income (BUG-0873, owner decision 3), drafted in lane v2-income, 2026-11-16; for the
+        owner.
